<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
To Whom It May Concern,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
Pursuant to ORS 192.311 et seq., I am requesting the following records:<o:p=
></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
All public records requests received by the Oregon Parks and Recreation Dep=
artment from January 1, 2023 to present, including for each: the date recei=
ved, the date of agency response, the method of production (electronic or p=
hysical mail), whether a fee was
 assessed, whether a fee waiver was requested, whether a fee waiver was gra=
nted, and whether the request was fulfilled in whole, in part, or denied.<o=
:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
All written policies, procedures, or guidelines governing the agency's resp=
onse to public records requests, including any internal guidance on product=
ion format, fee assessment, and timeline compliance.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
All records reflecting instances where the agency missed the statutory five=
-business-day response deadline under ORS 192.324, from January 1, 2023 to =
present.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
All records reflecting the involvement of the OPRD Director, OPRD Interim D=
irector, or OPRD Deputy Director in the review, approval, or direction of r=
esponses to public records requests from January 1, 2023 to present, includ=
ing any communications in which
 executive staff directed the content, timing, or format of a response.<o:p=
></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
All records reflecting communications between OPRD legal counsel and execut=
ive staff regarding public records requests, including any guidance on with=
holding, delaying, or limiting production of records.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
All records reflecting instances where OPRD legal counsel reviewed a public=
 records request prior to response, from January 1, 2023 to present.<o:p></=
o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
I request that responsive records be produced on a rolling basis as they ar=
e identified rather than held until the request is fully processed.<o:p></o=
:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
Please be advised that I expect all records potentially responsive to this =
request to be preserved immediately. Any destruction, deletion, modificatio=
n, or alteration of responsive records following receipt of this request ma=
y constitute spoliation and will
 be treated accordingly.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
If any record or portion of a record is withheld, I require the following f=
or each withheld item: the specific statutory exemption claimed, the date o=
f the record, the author, and all recipients. A blanket exemption claim is =
insufficient and will not be accepted
 as compliance.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
I am requesting a fee waiver on the grounds that this request serves the pu=
blic interest by enabling public oversight of agency compliance with Oregon=
 public records law. This request is not commercial in nature. Responsive r=
ecords will be used to inform and
 supplement a public archive documenting institutional conduct, accessible =
at oprdvolunteerabuse.org. Public access to this information advances trans=
parency and accountability in government.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>I am further requesting that all responsive records be produced electron=
ically in PDF or equivalent digital format and delivered to
<a href=3D"mailto:rsw@rswfire.com">rsw@rswfire.com</a>.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
Please confirm receipt of this request in writing within the statutory five=
-business-day window pursuant to ORS 192.324.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt=
;margin-left:0in">
